  "parts": [
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic managed metrics monitoring task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file query_metric_window.py using Microsoft/OpenAI.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] query_metric_window.py - queries recent datapoints for a named metric over a time window\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] aggregate_metric_stats.py - retrieves aggregated statistics for a metric over a time window\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] filter_metric_dimensions.py - queries metric data filtered by resource labels or dimensions\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] compare_metric_series.py - compares metric values for two resources or dimension filters over the same window\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] observability_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Metrics Monitoring\n6. [HELPER] observability_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Metrics Monitoring\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] metric_summary.py - Summarize recent metric trends or anomalies\n8. [LATER-STEP] metric_annotation_safety.py - Check free-text metric labels or annotations for unsafe text\n9. [LATER-STEP] dashboard_note_translate.py - Translate metric or dashboard notes for another locale\n10. [LATER-STEP] metrics_export_archive.py - Archive exported metric snapshots in managed object storage\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
